On 09/20/06 7:38 AM, kanze wrote:

> I seem to remember some way of modifying the way standard xterm
> displays colors, something in the .Xdefaults file, so I'll try
> that.  Or I'll just download the sources and modify them:-).

Put something like

XTerm*Color4: DodgerBlue

in ~/.Xresources, and then either restart your X server or do an

xrdb ~/.Xresources

to load it. Then xterm will always get a nice light blue that's much
easier to see on a black background (other colours are listed in
/usr/X11R6/lib/X11/rgb.txt)...

